  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations in Kentucky totaled $8B in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, obligating $7.3B of that total. Award activity shows 74,790 awards with an average award size of $107K. Obligations fell 23.2% year over year, following a multi-year range that peaked at $12.5B in FY23 and declined to $10.4B in FY25 before arriving at the current $8B level in FY26. Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers is the largest industry by obligations, receiving $5.5B. HUMANA GOVERNMENT BUSINESS INC likewise received $5.5B and is the largest vendor. The top buying agencies after the Department of Defense are the Department of the Treasury with $183M, the Department of Veterans Affairs with $135M, and the Department of Justice with $134M. The top industries after Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers include All Other Support Services at $513M and Other Heavy and Civil Engineering Construction at $368M.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies award the most federal contracts in Kentucky?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $7.3B in FY2026 to date. The Department of the Treasury obligated $183M, the Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $135M, and the Department of Justice obligated $134M. The General Services Administration, Department of Homeland Security, and Department of Agriculture follow with $56.1M, $44.2M, and $30.1M respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the largest contractors and which industries collect the most obligations?",
        "body": "HUMANA GOVERNMENT BUSINESS INC received $5.5B in FY2026 to date. LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION and THALLE - BAUER LLC follow with $511M and $345M. Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers received $5.5B, All Other Support Services received $513M, and Other Heavy and Civil Engineering Construction received $368M."
      }
    ]
  },
